            <ArticleTitle>When migraine is more than a headache. Stroke in a young patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>87-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stroke rarely occurs in a young patient with migraine. Nevertheless, vascular headache can lead to catastrophic neurologic consequences, and severe headache associated with persistent neurologic deficits poses a complex diagnostic problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
